<h1>Bubble Sort</h1>
<p>
    Bubble Sort is a sorting algorithm that is well-known for its simplicity.
    <br>
    <br>
    Bubble Sort loops through the array, 
    and at each step checks if the current element is less than the previous.
    If it is, then Bubble Sort swaps the two elements.
    Either way, it then continues to the next element.
    It does this until it reaches the end of the array, then it loops through the array again.
    Bubble Sort repeats this until it does not make any swaps during a loop, meaning the array is sorted.
    <br>
    <br>
    At the end of each loop the next largest element in the array is placed at the end.
    A common optimization, which this visualization uses, is to stop one step ealier each loop, 
    since the end of the array is already sorted.
    <br>
    <br>
    Bubble Sort is also well known for its slowness. 
    It performs much slower than other sorting algorithms.
    It is normally used for when an easy-to-write algorithm is needed, or to compare against other algorithms.
</p>

