<h2>Cocktail Shaker Sort</h2>
<p>
    Cocktail Shaker Sort, also called Cocktail Sort, Shaker Sort, or Shuffle Sort, 
    is a well-known variation of Bubble Sort.
    <br>
    <br>
    It works the same as Bubble Sort, but after reaching the end of the array, 
    it loops back to the beginning before starting over.
    While heading back to the beginning of the array, 
    it continues to swap the current and previous element (now the next element since it is traveling backwards),
    if they are out of order.
    <br>
    <br>
    Cocktail Shaker Sort places the next smallest element at the beginning of the array 
    as well as the next largest one at the end.
    A similar optimization as Bubble sort is often used, 
    where Cocktail Shaker Sort will start and stop looping one element sooner or later each time.
    As before, this visualization uses this optimization.
    <br>
    <br>
    On average Cocktail Shaker Sort is slightly quicker than Bubble Sort, 
    but it is still much slower than other algorithms.
</p>